{"author":"rebar review bot","author_email":"rebar-review-bot@rebar.solutions.navateam.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe plan-review gate's T1 (prior art) criterion is the only criterion that searches the\nweb. When that search returns nothing, the underlying `ddgs` library RAISES instead of\nreturning an empty list. rebar has no handler for that library's exception, so the\nexception escapes the tool, is classified as an LLM provider outage, and degrades the\nENTIRE plan review to an unsigned `INDETERMINATE` verdict. A review that costs roughly\n8 minutes of LLM time is discarded because a web search came back empty.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by reproduction)\n\nCall chain, at current tree lines:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py:502` sets `web_requested`; `:522` calls `web_search_capabilities`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:154-159` builds `WebSearch(native=..., local=duckduckgo_search_tool(...))`, passing pydantic-ai's tool straight through.\n- `pydantic_ai/common_tools/duckduckgo.py:60` awaits the client with NO exception handler.\n- `ddgs/ddgs.py:454` does `raise DDGSException(err or \"No results found.\")`.\n\n`grep -rn 'DDGSException|ddgs' src/rebar/` returns nothing: rebar has no handler anywhere.\n\nReproduced live, 2 failures in 3 attempts, terminating at `ddgs.py:454`. A backend probe\nshowed `auto` and `bing` returning results while `duckduckgo`, `google`, `brave`, and\n`mojeek` all raised; for a synthetic zero-result query every backend raised 3/3.\n\nrebar's handling of the escape, confirmed by running the classifier:\n\n```\nclassify -> ResolutionClass.NEEDS_INVESTIGATION,\n  diagnostic={'exception_type': 'DDGSException', 'message': 'No results found.'},\n  retryable=False\nraised -> LLMUnavailableError\n```\n\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:204` catches `LLMUnavailableError` and calls\n`_degraded_plan_review_verdict`, recording `llm_ran=False` and logging\n`llm-degrade NEEDS_INVESTIGATION on plan-review`. There is no retry, no per-criterion\nfallback, and no no-web review path.\n\n## The trap this fix must avoid\n\nA controlled probe proved that a genuinely empty result and a backend that failed are\nINDISTINGUISHABLE in the common case: an empty engine and an engine raising\n`DDGSException(\"No results found.\")` produce the same exception type, the same message,\nand no `__cause__` or `__context__`. Only a distinctive message such as a timeout or a\nbackend-specific error text can be told apart.\n\nTherefore a handler that simply swallows the exception and returns `[]` is NOT a fix. It\nwould make T1 conclude \"no prior art exists\" when the search actually failed, trading a\nloud failure for a quiet wrong answer that silently degrades review quality.\n\n## Impact\n\nEight open bugs are instances of this same defect, each carrying an identical session-log\npayload naming `DDGSException` / `No results found.`: `0b56-ad83`, `2b30-5d6f`,\n`2ced-55f3`, `602b-4a55`, `812d-7eba`, `8d53-4d0f`, `cb9c-61c8`, `ccd8-e843`.\n\n## Approach (decided)\n\nOwn the local web-search boundary inside rebar instead of passing pydantic-ai's raw tool\nthrough. In `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py`, `web_search_capabilities()` will build a\nrebar-owned local search callable that wraps the underlying client and catches\n`ddgs.exceptions.DDGSException` at that boundary only.\n\nBehaviour on catch, split by what is actually knowable:\n\n1. Message exactly `\"No results found.\"` - indistinguishable between true-empty and\n   backend-failed, so return an empty result list. T1 then reasons from \"no prior-art\n   results were returned\" and the review COMPLETES instead of being voided.\n2. Any other message, including timeouts and backend-specific errors - return an explicit\n   degraded marker result whose text states that web search was unavailable and quotes the\n   backend failure. T1 can then report that prior art could not be verified, rather than\n   asserting that none exists.\n\nNeither branch re-raises, so no web-search outcome can void a whole plan review again.\n\nThis is an in-process change on the tool path, with no dependency on any CI provider, so\nit behaves identically under `make verify`, under GitHub Actions, and under any other or\nno CI provider.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py` - the wrapper and its use in `web_search_capabilities`.\n- `tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py` - the red/green tests.\n\nOut of scope: retrying across backends, caching prior-art results, changing T1's prompt or\nits `suppress_types`, and re-triaging the eight related tickets (handled separately once\nthis lands).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 When the underlying client raises `DDGSException(\"No results found.\")`, rebar's local web-search tool RETURNS an empty result list rather than raising. Checked: a test monkeypatches the client to raise exactly that and asserts the tool returns an empty list and does not raise.\n- [ ] AC2 When the underlying client raises `DDGSException` with any other message, the tool returns an explicit degraded result whose text contains the backend failure message, and does not raise and does not return an empty list. Checked: a test monkeypatches the client to raise `DDGSException(\"backend exploded\")` and asserts the returned payload contains `backend exploded`.\n- [ ] AC3 `web_search_capabilities(web=True)` installs rebar's own wrapper as the local tool, not pydantic-ai's raw `duckduckgo_search_tool`, so the handler cannot be bypassed. Checked: a test asserts on the identity or provenance of the installed local tool.\n- [ ] AC4 The new tests FAIL before the change and PASS after it. Checked: capture the red output naming the propagated `DDGSException`, then the green output.\n- [ ] AC5 No test in this change performs a live network request. Checked: every test monkeypatches the client; the suite passes with networking unavailable.\n- [ ] AC6 `make verify` shows no failure other than the 17 known macOS-arm64 pandoc `Bad CPU type` failures, which are environmental.\n- [ ] AC7 The change lands on `main` through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n\n## Testing\n\nTargeted `pytest tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py`, then `make verify` in the change's\nown worktree. Expect exactly 17 pre-existing pandoc failures on macOS arm64; an 18th is\nreal and blocks the push."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789953863358001001,"uuid":"f7ec5e40-1d9b-4fcf-b5c6-f848d89b515f"}